00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.900
the arcade version, it's, you know, Sam said when I showed it to him, it's a completely

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:06.880
different game. Yeah.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:07.920
You know, it's really cool.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:09.440
It performs really well.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.460
It's obviously tight.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:16.020
There's, um, you know, there's a lot more visual cues as to what's going on in the atmosphere

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.160
and stuff like that, but I don't want to bash the game too much.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:23.560
So, you know, Sam was kind of getting into it earlier about these little details, but

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:26.380
I, I just really even appreciate the way the game starts.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.540
We got a cut scene. It's a cool cut scene.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:32.060
How many cut scenes have we had in NES games so far?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.540
Yeah, there's not been many, but Commando had one, right?

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.860
I mean, sort of. Sort of.

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:36.520
Well, it's just the helicopter dropping you off.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:37.980
Yeah. Well, then it's part of the game.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.520
And Russian Attack has several.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:45.440
Yeah. And, um, also didn't, um, Kung Fu have the save Sylvia thing?

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:47.360
Yeah. That was like after the first level.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:48.400
It was the second level. Yeah.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.920
That's when you get your mission.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.060
Like, oh yeah, that's one. Yeah.

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.040
We forgot to tell you, this is what you're doing.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:57.520
I like the idea that in the first level, you're just training in the dojo and then all

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.020
of a sudden it's like, you're like, wait, what?

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.980
Yeah. But I thought that, that, that, that intro cut scene thing was kind of cool.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:09.660
And I think like, you know, the way that, uh, two player is implemented is like a nice

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:14.320
touch because Commando is just like character, you know, player one goes, they died.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:19.580
Then player two goes in Ikari Warriors, even on the NES version, two players playing on the

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:21.900
same screen. Like that's, that's a very cool thing.

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:25.940
And Sam and I got an opportunity to play that and had a lot more fun with that version of

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:28.300
it. Yeah. I think that was a lot of fun.

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:32.240
I think it makes more sense for, you know, at least two people to take God and army.

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:40.380
Yeah. I do always think that this kind of multiplayer is better than what Commando did where you

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:42.260
alternate. Yeah.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.140
I like the idea that it's a game where you're playing together.

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:45.980
Yeah.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:52.080
But to go back to Sean talking about the, uh, the twin stick part of it, there is a, you

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:55.600
know, and it's a very small thing, but Sam opened my eyes to this about when you're in

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.660
the tank, you can control how you shoot.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:04.880
Yes. Yeah. By, by, by, by stopping and then adjusting and then going again.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:09.500
I think that's cool that they, it's, it's, it's a problem.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.760
It's the solving of a problem, but it's not elegant.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:16.020
But again, I think if it was just a tank game, it'd be more fun.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.540
Cause I, I, when I was in the tank, I was having the most fun.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:23.640
I agree, but I, I don't think I would still, I really still don't think I would like this

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.640
game very much. It changes the game too much for me.

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:30.220
Like, you know, if you just like for me, even like playing in the tank was like, it

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.260
was like a cool touch.

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:32.860
I wouldn't want to play the whole game in the tank.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:37.360
I guess that's fair. I guess it's just cause the, the walking around was so, like, was so janky.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:38.500
You're supposed to be an Ikari warrior.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:42.580
But the only reason I feel like I agree with the tank thing is because yeah, I really didn't

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.480
like walking around.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:45.540
Yeah. I felt like it controlled very poorly.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:46.540
Yeah. And you're frustrated.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.840
I guess it's just the tanks just control better.

00:15:48.980 --> 00:15:53.120
What's everybody's thoughts on the difficulty, the difficulty of this game starts off very

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:55.540
difficult, but I think you can learn it pretty fast.

00:15:55.540 --> 00:16:00.660
But then you like, you get to a point in the game where you're like, I should be done

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:02.200
by now. Yeah. I agree.

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.840
It is impressively long.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:08.680
This, this whole game get, I mean, does there, does it tell you that you, you got through

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.120
stage one? Like it stops the game.

00:16:10.220 --> 00:16:11.660
I could not get through stage one.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:13.360
I kept thinking cause it keeps tricking you.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:14.680
It keeps thinking like, Oh, here's a wall.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:15.640
This is going to be the boss.

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:16.800
And like, Oh, I beat that stuff.

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:18.620
I keep going. And there's like a tank.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:19.860
And I'm like, Oh, I'll beat this.

00:16:19.980 --> 00:16:25.460
And I found one of the old cheats, which was as soon as you lose your last life, you can

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:30.860
just hit it. Continue by going like a, a, b, b, a, a, cause it's one of those like a, b, b, a, or something

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:31.740
is continue.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:35.260
And I kept doing that every time I died.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:41.780
And I could not even just through sheer force of will get to the end of the first level.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.780
There was a point where I started to wonder, are there levels in this game or is this just

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.120
a really long level?

00:16:47.440 --> 00:16:51.200
So the way that it works is, uh, you're, you're both kind of right.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.760
Uh, there's two areas in the game total.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:55.860
They are incredibly long.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:01.500
I would put them in length to like a full game of super Mario brothers, you know, like,

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.420
like that's how long these, these levels are.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:08.120
And so there's kind of like, you know, they call them area one and area two.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.660
Wow. And creative.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:16.000
Yeah. Area one is like, you know, kind of storming up to like, you have to go through the jungle

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.580
into the waters, take the helicopter, do all this stuff.

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:25.000
And then area two is more like you're at the base now and it's like really confined spaces.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:27.860
And it's, it's even more difficult.

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:31.840
It seems like such a waste that it's so hard to get there.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:35.700
Like, I feel like most of the people that get this game are never going to get there.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:40.580
Sure. But I think that, that, you know, it also offers something, something different and

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:46.920
unique in the sense of how it handles like a level, like it's just an incredibly long

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:47.780
level. Yeah.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:50.640
Even though I didn't get through any of that, I give them, I give them props for that.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:53.600
Cause I kind of, just as you are describing that, it sounds kind of cool.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:57.800
Like, Oh, I'm kind of actually traversing this environment and seeing like the progression

00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.200
of like, now I'm in the swampy area, I'm in the jungle area.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:03.860
It's like a point A to B thing that you can like very clearly see.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:08.260
Yeah. I think it's kind of cool that like every time I got a little bit further, you know, like

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:11.860
when the first time I saw the helicopter, I was like, Whoa, you could do a helicopter too.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:13.040
Like that was cool.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:15.000
You know? So yeah, the sun says that.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.360
So yeah. All that stuff is really cool.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:22.540
And the, the, it's the little details in this game that make me like turn around on it a

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.680
little bit, but that's why, you know, I wanted to start with like the complaints first, because

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:31.700
I think that like, it's very easy to talk about all these nice little details that the

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:35.800
game does, but you have to remember like all of its shortcomings too.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.940
Any straight thoughts

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:35.120
Any thoughts on this one? I wasn't sure what some of the power-ups were.

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:38.620
We figured out that one kills all the enemies on the screen.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.600
Yeah, the K. What's the P?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.040
I don't know. I don't know what the rest of them are.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.280
But there's also an icon of a pistol.

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:47.920
Oh, there's the icon.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.180
Honestly, I have no idea.

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:52.060
And there's some that could be rockets if you're in the tank,

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.440
and some that do. I'm not really sure.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.260
You asked this question without knowing the answer?

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.860
Yeah, that's what questions are for.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.020
That wasn't a straight question.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:20:01.160
It was a straight thought. All right, here's a straight thought.

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:04.300
I thought that the dying animation was way too annoying.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:07.140
Yeah. Oh, I'm spinning and I can't get up.

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:09.400
I think we're going to say the same thing.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:11.320
But when you die the last time,

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:13.620
it's like here's 30 seconds for you to think about it

00:20:13.620 --> 00:20:14.820
before we tell you it's a game over.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:17.160
Yeah, exactly. 30 seconds where nobody's on the screen.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.580
I mean, that's just for you to put in any code that you want.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:21.920
Oh, yeah, I didn't know there was a code.

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.320
Right, but not knowing that there's a code,

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.680
that's how I felt too. I was like, can I just start over?

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:27.940
Do I have to hit reset?

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.940
Maybe it's to encourage people to just press buttons

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:32.100
to try and do something.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:34.180
That's true. Maybe they'll discover it.

00:20:34.220 --> 00:20:35.340
Maybe they'll find the code, yeah.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.160
But I was actually going to bring up something different, Joe,

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:39.880
weirdly enough. I thought we were in sync.

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.760
When you're in the helicopter or the tank,

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:44.440
how do you get out?

00:20:44.480 --> 00:20:47.640
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah. It says in the manual that you press A and then B,

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.360
which works sometimes.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:54.720
But if you get shot enough that your tank is about to explode

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:58.240
and you do it, I felt like it worked 25% of the time.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.360
Yeah, I died a lot.

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:03.380
I was almost afraid of the tank at some point

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:05.220
just because I'm like, I'm going to get in that death trap.

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:10.380
I guess it's a very realistic way to represent you

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:12.360
getting trapped in a burning vehicle.

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:14.580
Yeah, sometimes you can get out, sometimes you can't.

00:21:14.980 --> 00:21:16.400
Also, I'm not sure if it's a glitch,

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.760
but I saw in our two-player game,

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:23.220
I saw Sam run over someone and they died,

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:24.520
and I thought that was a nice touch.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.780
I did it twice, so I don't think it's a glitch.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:27.900
I'm not sure if I took damage.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:29.180
When you're in the tank, it's like you're a powerhouse.

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:31.920
I don't know if I took damage from that, but I don't know.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.780
I don't care if you did. I'm saying it's nice that at least the person died, too.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.820
Yeah, that's nice. Nice.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.140
It just went face-to-face with a tank,

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.080
you know how annoying it would be

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.480
if they came out the other side?

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:45.440
Like, I'm not done with you, buddy.

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.560
A ton of damage. Tank starts on fire.

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:52.220
And I would say that there's some nice set pieces

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:53.700
throughout this game. I like those bridges.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:54.980
Yeah, I think it's interesting

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.380
because it makes you think about how you're going to attack.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:02.320
You know, there's people across the river from you

00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:04.080
and there's a bridge and you're in a tank.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.340
You can be like, all right,

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:07.860
I can either cross the bridge on my tank

00:22:07.860 --> 00:22:10.960
or get out of the tank and cross the river as a person.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:13.220
So hearing you guys describe it,

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:14.660
I'm like, wow, this sounds fun.

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:16.120
Yeah. But then I got to remind myself,

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:17.780
no, I had a terrible time with this game.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.380
That's what I'm saying. It's tricky. But it sounds so fun.

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.660
I think it could have been a great game.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:24.320
And it is a great game on the arcade version.

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:25.860
I highly recommend the arcade version.

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:26.820
It's a good game.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:28.800
Like, don't get me wrong. I'm just saying that, like,

00:22:29.060 --> 00:22:30.600
it's so easy to talk about, like,

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:31.960
all the cool things about this game

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:33.320
and then remember, but wait a minute,

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:34.580
the controls stink.

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:36.000
It's easy to die.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:38.160
I barely can shoot my gun.

00:22:38.480 --> 00:22:40.060
You know, it's, in theory,

00:22:40.240 --> 00:22:42.280
these things work, but then they don't

00:22:42.280 --> 00:22:44.160
when you pop in the game and turn it on.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:46.020
Yeah. Exactly. It's a near miss.

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:47.620
Yeah. But don't worry,

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.600
because we got two more Ikari Warrior games

00:22:50.600 --> 00:22:53.040
coming up in the NES lifespan.

00:22:53.040 --> 00:22:55.760
We have Ikari 2, Victory Road.

00:22:56.540 --> 00:22:57.980
Some Pokemon references.

00:22:59.860 --> 00:23:02.060
And Ikari 3, The Rescue.

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:04.320
Which, don't confuse it with

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:05.700
the rescue operation

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:06.840
that you're doing in this one.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:08.540
Oh, okay. Yeah, I mean, at the end of the game,

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:10.320
you do rescue General Kawasaki,

00:23:10.400 --> 00:23:11.740
so it's like, I don't know why

00:23:12.200 --> 00:23:13.880
they're saying you don't rescue him,

00:23:13.980 --> 00:23:14.840
and, like, who knows.

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:16.560
But later that same day.

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:19.020
Thank you for neeming that out.

00:23:19.680 --> 00:23:20.920
All right, let's get into

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:22.580
the Essential Games List.

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:26.700
All right, it's time for

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:27.840
the Essential Games List.

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:29.140
And if you don't know what that is,

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:30.540
check the older episodes.

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:32.780
No, I kid. And yes, I'm reading

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:34.020
a prerecorded script,

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:36.760
only I'm not. To confuse people,

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:38.260
this is the...

00:23:38.260 --> 00:23:41.040
This is how the Essential Games List works.

00:23:41.200 --> 00:23:42.600
We just kind of go around

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:43.700
and we confuse people

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:44.960
with how we feel about this game.

00:23:45.060 --> 00:23:45.920
We say we don't like it,

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:46.880
we say we do like it.

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:47.960
It doesn't matter in the end,

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:49.180
because all that really matters

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:50.720
is if you vote yay or nay

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:52.200
for the Essential Games List.

00:23:52.340 --> 00:23:53.320
But we're not talking about

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:54.740
are these games essential for the NES?

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:55.960
We're not talking about 1987.

00:23:55.960 --> 00:23:57.680
I'm not talking about 2017.

00:23:57.700 --> 00:23:59.180
I'm talking about 2018.

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:01.820
Are these games worth playing today

00:24:01.820 --> 00:24:03.220
when you have access

00:24:03.220 --> 00:24:04.720
to every other game

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:05.900
that's ever come out?

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:07.740
Clearly you have time

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:09.420
because you're listening to the podcast.

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:12.760
So let's see how you guys feel about this.

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.620
Sean. All right.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:20.360
I don't see as many pros

00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:22.440
to this game as my colleagues here.

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:25.420
I do like that they tried

00:24:25.420 --> 00:24:27.800
to jazz up the commando version.

00:24:28.000 --> 00:24:29.940
I mean, sorry. They tried to jazz up

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:32.700
the commando-like genre

00:24:33.320 --> 00:24:35.400
with vehicles and, you know,

00:24:36.040 --> 00:24:37.840
tanks and helicopters are cool.

00:24:38.800 --> 00:24:41.420
And I like the long level lengths,

00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:43.720
but I don't like long levels

00:24:43.720 --> 00:24:45.760
of frustrating gameplay.

00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:48.040
And that's all I really felt

00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:49.080
while I was playing this.

00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:50.600
So it's a nay for me.

00:24:50.600 --> 00:24:51.980
That's a nay for Sean.

00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:53.500
Remember, you need two votes

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:55.080
to be in the Essential Games list.

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:58.420
Sam. I really like this game.

00:24:58.580 --> 00:24:59.960
I had a lot of fun with it.

00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:01.380
I didn't know that there was

00:25:01.380 --> 00:25:03.980
the continue code that you can do,

00:25:04.100 --> 00:25:05.040
but knowing that now

